    "concept": "Contrast enhancement alone cannot distinguish radiation necrosis from recurrent tumor because both disrupt the blood-brain barrier. Perfusion MRI separates them physiologically: recurrent tumor is hypervascular (high rCBV), while radiation necrosis is hypovascular (low rCBV). MR spectroscopy and PET support the same logic (high choline or FDG uptake = tumor). Biopsy is the gold standard when imaging is equivocal.",
